			],
			"Message": "fix(Maintain): Implement guard disarm mechanism to preserve modified configs\n\nThis commit advances the Maintain submodule to a12cf4f5, introducing an \"armed\" state to the Guard RAII pattern in the Maintain build system.\n\nPreviously, the Guard would always restore the original file on drop, regardless of whether the build succeeded or failed. This meant that successful builds would have their modified configuration files (Cargo.toml, Tauri config) reverted, causing unnecessary overhead.\n\nThe changes add:\n- An `Armed` boolean field to the `Guard` struct that controls whether restoration occurs\n- A `disarm()` method to explicitly prevent restoration after successful operations\n- Modified `Drop` implementation to check `self.Armed` before restoring\n\nIn `Process.rs`, both `CargoGuard` and `ConfigGuard` are now disarmed after successful build completion, preserving the modified configuration files in place.\n\nThis ensures that successful builds leave the project in a usable state without needing to re-apply configuration changes, while still providing safety via automatic restoration on failure (panic or unexpected exit).\n\nAlso advances the Sky submodule to 95eaf2b5 for consistency with the latest UI component layer.",
			"SHA": "e7442d0b23d4ebc614273710edbc06febf171c64"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-03T11:27:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				6
			],
			"Message": "chore(Monorepo): Synchronize multiple elements with naming consistency and updates\n\nThis commit advances submodules to their latest commits, introducing cross-element naming standardization and dependency updates.\n\n## Naming Convention Standardization\n\n### Air: Singular Field Naming\n- Renamed plural fields to singular in `ApplicationState` (e.g., `Connections` → `Connection`, `ActiveRequests` → `ActiveRequest`)\n- Updated `PerformanceMetrics` fields (`TotalRequests` → `TotalRequest`)\n- Updated `ConnectionHealthReport` fields (`TotalConnections` → `TotalConnection`)\n- Propagated changes to Binary.rs and AirVinegRPCService.rs\n\n### Grove: Namespace Renaming\n- Renamed `Commands` → `CommandNamespace` to match VS Code API namespace pattern\n- Renamed `Languages` → `LanguageNamespace` for consistency\n- Renamed `Extensions` → `ExtensionNamespace`\n- Fixed `CreateFilesParams` → `CreateFileParams` for singular parameter semantics\n\n### Mountain: Singular Naming & Thread Safety\n- Renamed collection fields to singular (`MaxConnections` → `MaxConnection`, `ActiveConnections` → `ActiveConnection`)\n- Renamed `PendingUserInterfaceRequests` → `PendingUserInterfaceRequest`\n- Renamed `Extensions` → `ScannedExtensionCollection`\n- **Thread Safety**: Replaced unsafe `static mut` with `RwLock` in `Scheme.rs` for `SERVICE_REGISTRY`\n- Updated build configuration: binary entry point moved to `Source/Library.rs` for mobile builds\n\n## Dependency & Build Updates\n\n### Common: Dependency Bump\n- Bumped `actions/upload-artifact` from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0\n\n### Output: Save Commit\n- Advanced to latest commit with signed-off changes\n\n### Worker: Build Artifacts\n- Rebuilt Service Worker entry point, CSS loading module, policy handler, and registration logic\n- Ensures consistency with current Wind and Sky component versions\n\nImpact: Achieves naming consistency across Air, Grove, and Mountain elements, improves thread safety in Mountain's `land://` protocol handler, and updates build artifacts.",
			"SHA": "78ebab100c495a9b636eaf6897150df2f280e71f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-27T13:26:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Update submodule to latest commit\n\nThis commit advances the Mountain submodule to d4becf1b23ceb5e8ebda28bab28fe6dd23bf7e3e, incorporating the latest changes from the Mountain element. The update includes the \"save\" commit with Signed-off-by Nikola Hristov, representing recent work in the native backend.\n\nThis submodule synchronization ensures the monorepo root remains aligned with the latest Mountain backend implementation.",
			"SHA": "860269f3531ffeeaca50174996ab35f2af9f4b5d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-27T13:20:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Monorepo): Clean up dead code and improve code quality across multiple elements\n\nThis commit performs routine maintenance and cleanup across five elements of the Land ecosystem, reducing compiler warnings and improving overall code quality.\n\n## Air: Dead Code Cleanup & Lint Attributes\n- Prefixed unused parameters with underscore (`_config`, `_timeout_duration`)\n- Added crate-level `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` for existing naming conventions\n- Added `#[allow(dead_code)]` to intentionally unused functions and structs\n- Removed unused imports and cleaned up TODO placeholder comments\n\n## Grove: Unused Variable & Import Cleanup\n- Cleaned up unused variables across all modules (API, Binary, Common, Host, Protocol, Services, Transport, WASM)\n- Added `#[allow(dead_code)]` to structs reserved for future use\n- Removed unused imports (`Context`, `Serialize`, `Bytes`)\n- Simplified unnecessary `mut` declarations\n\n## Maintain: Binary Entry Point Restructuring\n- Created dedicated `Source/main.rs` as binary entry point\n- Separated library code from binary source following standard Rust conventions\n- Updated `Cargo.toml` to point to new binary path\n\n## Mountain: Thread Safety & Code Cleanup\n- Replaced unsafe `static mut` with `RwLock` in `Scheme.rs` for SERVICE_REGISTRY and CACHE\n- Added module-level lint attributes to suppress warnings\n- Removed unused imports across multiple provider files\n- Standardized struct field formatting and documentation\n\n## Wind: Dependency Updates\n- Bumped `actions/upload-artifact` from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0\n- Bumped `@effect/language-service` from 0.76.0 to 0.77.0\n\nImpact: Eliminates compiler warnings, prepares codebase for future development, and updates dependencies.",
			"SHA": "f2cc2668e87eafba717c92f78c66d2bc5065bac3"
		}
	],
